      {"type": "title", "bbox": [50, 165, 300, 178], "detailed_index": 6, "confirmed_index": 5, "title_level": 1,
       "text": "ABSTRACT"},
      {"type": "text", "bbox": [50, 180, 300, 420], "detailed_index": 7, "confirmed_index": 6,
       "text": "ABSTRACT: Positive allosteric modulators (PAMs) of the dopamine D1 receptor are an alternative to orthosteric agonists. Starting from hit compound 3, a structure-activity relationship study led to the identification of UCM-1306 (26), which potentiates the dopamine response at the human D 1 receptor, shows good PAMPA permeability and low hERG inhibition, and is orally bioavailable."},
      {"type": "image_body", "bbox": [320, 150, 560, 312], "detailed_index": null, "confirmed_index": 3,
       "merged_from": [3, 4], "caption_text": "Table of contents graphic", "merged_img_path": "merged_images/p000_g003.jpg"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_idx": 1,
    "page_size": [612.0, 792.0],
    "para_blocks": [
      {"type": "title", "bbox": [50, 60, 300, 75], "detailed_index": 0, "confirmed_index": 0, "title_level": 1,
       "text": "INTRODUCTION"},
      {"type": "text", "bbox": [50, 80, 300, 400], "detailed_index": 1, "confirmed_index": 1,
       "text": "The dopamine D1 receptor (D1R) is a class A G protein-coupled receptor that is highly expressed in the striatum and prefrontal cortex. Enhancing D1R signaling is a therapeutic strategy for cognitive impairment in Parkinson's disease and schizophrenia."},
      {"type": "list", "bbox": [320, 80, 560, 200], "detailed_index": 2, "confirmed_index": 2,
       "text": ""}
    ]
  },
  {
